url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-11T12:34:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T12:34:35Z","body":"https://commits.webkit.org/313593@main wpt.fyi is only occasionally updated.\n\nWhat seems weird/silly is that the restriction on `<url>` is not also applied to `<image>` then. It would make sense for that to be consistent.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4680592743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4680718089","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946#issuecomment-4680718089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946","id":4680718089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABFv4XCQ","user":{"login":"emilio","id":1323194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjMxOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1323194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio","html_url":"https://github.com/emilio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-11T12:48:57Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T12:48:57Z","body":"Well, but `<image>` is a super set and it makes sense to maybe have something like `data-bg=\"linear-gradient(..)\"` or so, right?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4680718089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4791362909","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946#issuecomment-4791362909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946","id":4791362909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABHZZlXQ","user":{"login":"css-meeting-bot","id":27466577,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDY2NTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27466577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/css-meeting-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T16:14:00Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T16:14:00Z","body":"The CSS Working Group just discussed `[css-values] attr() banning type(<url>) is kind of arbitrary.`.\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;kbabbitt> scribe+ kbabbitt<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: this came up during some interop2026 work<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... seems like we decided a while ago to ban url type on attr<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... but didn't do anything on image which is a strict superset<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... concern was a bit theoretical in terms of computed urls not internationalizing well<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... any concern that applies to url applies to image<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... don't think it's particularly worth special casing url here, not easy to do<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... not easy to ??? where concern would apply<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... would make more sense to not apply any of those<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... don't think it was realized that you could get around this with image<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... feels kind of silly to ban url() for that if you can just use image()<br>\n&lt;astearns> s/???/get a string displayed/<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: I don't have a strong opinion here<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... banning url in attr seems like an easier change to make since attr is relatively new<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... do we thinnk there are instances of image in url that we would have compat problems with?<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: url tainting already takes care of security issues this would bring<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... mostly for things that don't load as urls<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... images useful in attr, could imagine background for example<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: so concern is that attr can be used in a way where we're displaying the parameter as opposed to the thing it's resolving to?<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: yes, and since computed urls get ascii encoded that's a problem<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... don't think it's a realistic concern, need to put parens around url anyway, why would you display that<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... computed url is function not string<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... so I don't think it's going to cause any i18n problems realistically<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... so it's silly to ban it especially if image is banned<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: makes sense to have consistency but anne seems against having it in attr<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: we can try to get anne's opinion, I don't see the big concern<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: I don't think we should resolve on anything today if we're not having that side of the argument represented<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... anne does show up for forms meetings, could maybe sneak it in there<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: reason I'm pusing to resolve is it impacts interoop<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> ... seems like a sad behavior to implement to be honest<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: anyone else with a strong opinion either way? should we try to push back on banning url in attr?<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> emilio: action item from fantasai or someone from webkit to get a yes/no?<br>\n&lt;lea> +1 for unbanning it from a DX perspective but it's not a strong opinion<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> fantasai: I just pinged anne on slack<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> astearns: let's take back to issue and hopefully get an opinion soon<br>\n</details>\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4791362909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4791489788","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946#issuecomment-4791489788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13946","id":4791489788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABHZhU_A","user":{"login":"annevk","id":1544111,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NDQxMTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1544111?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk","html_url":"https://github.com/annevk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/annevk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T16:29:47Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T16:29:47Z","body":"What does `attr(x type(<url>))` imply for the serialized form? Will you always get `url()` wrapping _x_? I would agree that makes it less Western-centric as that's not readily understandable as a URL.\n\nAnd what did @tabatkins mean with https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5079#issuecomment-4331159753, in particular:\n\n> Removing (for now) `attr(... type(<url>)` just means that you can't put an attribute value directly into a spot where CSS expects a URL, but that's already intentionally disallowed when getting the attr value as a string, to avoid exfiltration attacks.\n\nI'm pretty sure I was previously convinced there's no security issue here, but now I'm less sure.\n\nPerhaps given the churn we should exclude this specific test from Interop.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4791489788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.c